    "title": "Penn State blows 17-point lead in 24-20 loss to Wisconsin in Big Ten opener [updated] - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rich Scarcella rscarcella@readingeagle.com ,\n9 hours ago STATE COLLEGE – Penn State was on its way to a victory in Matt Campbell’s first Big Ten game as the head coach, building a 17-point lead over Wisconsin Saturday night. The 13th-ranked Nittany Lions still led by 10 points in the fourth quarter before everything suddenly went haywire. Read full article",
